A||||11||Alex2004||Mom just boguht a 93 Jag Vanden Plas, but now it won't start!!||||8||
Z||000000||Alex2004||01-09-2001||10:33 PM||||Today we bought a 1993 Jaguar Vanden Plas, we had been looking at it for abot 2 weeks.  Today we finally got it and when we came home, me and mom shut it off and went inside to get some stuff before we leave again. And so we got back in it and now it won't start. The dealer seems to think it's a security thing because when you unlock it, it sometimes gives you this fast beeping sound. we had the sales man come out and look at it and he still couldn't figure it out. And so we tried all sorts of stuff and it still won't start. Has anyone worked on/had a jag with this problem and can give me any Ideas of what to do? PLEASE LET ME KNOW, thanks...<BR>Alex...   PS: or just give me any advice you think could help!||||reg||8
Z||000001||fierospeeder||01-10-2001||01:20 AM||||is the car cranking, "starter"?<P>check in the owners manual for anything like a automatic fuel shutoff release button, like on the ford.  Just a guess.  <P>If its some security thing, try to see if theres any fuses blown.  <P>If theres a schrader valve on the car, try pressing it to see if any fuel is coming out, NOTE dont smoke while doing this.  If you got a timing light, try cranking it and see if you get the timing light to make some light.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||01-10-2001||01:43 AM||||This particular Jag may not have this but mine did and it drove me crazy! They have some sort of fuel shut-off valve that is intended to stop the flow of fuel in case of a wreck. But sometime hitting a pothole hard or even slamming a door hard can cause it! I sold my Jag about 5 years ago and can't remember the details. It is an easy fix though if you know what you are looking for.<P>If your car just spins and spins but doesn't even try to fire, this could be the cause...<P>Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||01-10-2001||12:54 PM||||Jags r notorious for electrical problems. It def could be alarm sys related, if someone wired in some kind of fuel shutoff or ignition kill. good luck. You might try to find the previous owners name and number and ask.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||01-10-2001||12:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>Jags r notorious for electrical problems. It def could be alarm sys related, if someone wired in some kind of fuel shutoff or ignition kill. good luck. You might try to find the previous owners name and number and ask.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>if you dont have any luck, heres email for a friend i know who restores jags, he has a 88 VandenPlas i just painted, <P>wickhamaudio@juno.com<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex2004||01-10-2001||08:39 PM||||Ok, thanks for the info. Well i looked through the manual and seen the fuel shut off sensor by the door for side impacts. The guy from the dealer checked that, the car at first would start but just putter, and then about 2 hours later the salesman/owner of the company came out and couldn't figure it out, since it was less than an hour of purchase they had a tow truck come out and tow it to OKC where the Jaguar dealers are and it is getting fixed.  So i never had time to check the forum and try some of the stuff yuo guys told me to do <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> But thanks for the information! I'll let you all know what the actual problem was when we get it back! But Thanks again!  <P>Alex...||||reg||4
